var scopes_default = "---\nlayout: article\ntitle: Resource scopes\ndescription: Learn how Appwrite Firewall scopes rules to the project API, a Function, or a Site, and where each scope is enforced.\n---\n\nEvery Firewall rule has a **resource type** that limits which traffic the rule can match. Scopes keep API-wide policies separate from policies for a single function or site.\n\n# Scope types {% #scope-types %}\n\n| Resource type | Applies to | Resource ID |\n|---------------|------------|-------------|\n| **API** | Project Appwrite API traffic (`/v1/...`) | Not required (stored empty) |\n| **Functions** | Public/edge traffic for one function | Function ID required |\n| **Sites** | Public/edge traffic for one site | Site ID required |\n\n# Where rules are enforced {% #where-rules-are-enforced %}\n\n- **API** rules are enforced on requests to your project's Appwrite API. This is the scope to use for Auth, Databases, Storage, and other `/v1` services.\n- **Functions** and **Sites** rules are stored on the project and applied to that function's or site's **public traffic** on the Appwrite Network edge.\n- Function and site rules do **not** block Console or Appwrite **management API** calls used to create, update, or deploy those resources. A deny rule on a function will not stop `GET /v1/functions/{id}` from a valid API key or the Console.\n\n{% info title=\"Pick the right scope\" %}\nTo protect SDK and client calls into Appwrite services, use **API**. To protect a deployed function URL or site hostname, use **Functions** or **Sites** with that resource selected.\n{% /info %}\n\n# When to use API {% #when-to-use-api %}\n\nUse **API** for project-wide API controls:\n\n- Block abusive client IPs across Auth, Databases, Storage, and other API services\n- Rate limit a shared path prefix such as `/v1`\n- Deny traffic from specific countries for the whole project API\n\n# When to use Functions {% #when-to-use-functions %}\n\nUse **Functions** when only one function's public traffic should be protected or exempted:\n\n- Rate limit a public webhook function\n- Deny non-`POST` methods on an HTTP-triggered function endpoint\n- Bypass Firewall checks for a trusted caller IP on that function only\n\nSelect the function in the create wizard. The rule appears under the **Functions** tab, grouped by that function.\n\n# When to use Sites {% #when-to-use-sites %}\n\nUse **Sites** for a single deployed web app's public traffic:\n\n- Redirect a deprecated path on one site\n- Deny admin paths on a marketing site\n- Rate limit form submission paths for one site\n\nSelect the site in the create wizard. The rule appears under the **Sites** tab.\n\n# Tabs in the Console {% #tabs-in-the-console %}\n\nThe Firewall page filters the list by scope tab. Creating a rule from a tab preselects that resource type. You can change the type in the create wizard or later when [updating](/docs/products/firewall/update) the rule.\n\n{% arrow_link href=\"/docs/products/firewall/create\" %}\nCreate a rule\n{% /arrow_link %}\n";
export { scopes_default as default };
